@startuml conditional_create_retry
!theme cyborg
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam backgroundColor #0b1018
skinparam defaultFontColor #e6edf7
skinparam ArrowColor #a9b8ca
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
title Why is a retry after a lost receipt safe? Conditional create of one Observation
participant COMMUNICATION
participant "WIFI\n(verified TLS 1.3)" as WIFI
participant "FHIR server" as Server
note over COMMUNICATION
 Frozen once before the first request: body bytes and
 identifier <server-device-id>:<measurement-end-UTC>.
 Every attempt sends exactly these bytes.
end note
COMMUNICATION -> WIFI : attempt 1: POST /Observation\nIf-None-Exist: identifier=urn%3Astethoscope%3Ameasurement|<identifier>
WIFI -> Server : request
Server -> Server : no match: create and commit the resource
Server -->x WIFI : 201 Created (lost: reset or receipt timeout)
WIFI --> COMMUNICATION : no complete receipt
COMMUNICATION -> COMMUNICATION : lost receipt is retryable; cancel and quiesce,\nthen 2 s gap if budget remains
COMMUNICATION -> WIFI : attempt 2: new connection setup (SNTP, DNS, TCP, TLS)\nthen identical POST, identical identifier and body
WIFI -> Server : request
alt One existing match
 Server -> Server : search finds the committed resource; nothing created
 Server --> WIFI : 200 OK
 WIFI --> COMMUNICATION : receipt: result Sent, no readback
else Terminal rejection
 Server --> WIFI : 412 (multiple matches), unsupported conditional create,\nauthentication or configuration error, other non-success status
 WIFI --> COMMUNICATION : terminal: no further attempt, no unconditional POST
 COMMUNICATION -> COMMUNICATION : DELIVERY_FAILURE; result visibly lost
else Retryable failure (5xx, timeout, lost receipt) until attempts or deadline run out
 COMMUNICATION -> COMMUNICATION : 4 attempts used or Stop + 10 s reached:\nDELIVERY_FAILURE; result visibly lost
end
note over COMMUNICATION, Server
 No delayed queue: a lost result is never resent, also not after the server recovers.
 A result that never gets a qualifying clock anchor sends no request: SERVER_CONNECTION_FAILURE at the deadline.
 Duplicate prevention follows the FHIR R4 conditional-create rules; whether the deployed
 HAPI FHIR server returns 200 for the existing match is unverified (integration evidence pending).
end note
@enduml
